Z||000000||reddog||11-09-2001||08:26 PM||||Does anyone have access to a diagram of the fuel injection system for an 86 GT. An exploded diagram of the intake system would be very helpful as well as any info that could be given on replacing  injectors. Also I still don't understand the cold start injector (IE it's location ,what it looks like,how it works, and how to check and replace it. I have just bought new injectors for my GT and plan to install them myself. However, I really don't know much about the fuel injection on my 2.8. Please help!!!!<BR>BTW I checked the haynes manual but it is very vague and doesn't even mention a cold start injector anywhere in the book. Is the factory service manual any better? Can anyone scan the instruction for me. Thanks reddog<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||11-09-2001||09:07 PM||||A bit about the cold start injector.<P>This circuit is activated only in the crank mode.  The power is supplied directly from the starter solenoid and only "ON" in the crank mode.  The system is controlled by a cold start fuel injection switch which provides a ground path for the valve during cranking when ever engine coolant is below 95 deg f.  <BR>The manual says it is not ECM controlled, I can not find a wiring schematic either.<P>Pete<p>[This message has been edited by PBJ (edited 11-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gary W||11-09-2001||09:40 PM||||The cold start valve is hidden behind the distributor. Standing behind the car, follow the intake plenum to the right (starting from throttle body) until you get to a vacuum nipple. Straight down, there is a small metal tube (mine is white) connected to the fuel rail. Cold start valve is at the other end of the tube. It is powered by the starter solenoid during cranking, if the coolant temp is below 95F. I have the '86 factory manual, and can scan some things if you want, but I dont see any test procedure for the valve. Looks like if the engine starts cold, the valve is OK. E-mail me if you want some info out of the book - good diagrams.||||reg||1
